# The CPQ's internal entrance, for colleagues. Add these blocks to the Caddyfile of
# the planning tool's Caddy (planningstool-caddy), which listens on 10.16.12.4 only
# (the planning tool's public IP, Sleeve only in the NSG, rules 121-123).
# That Caddy must be on the network cpq-net:
#   - in the planning tool's compose, under that Caddy:   networks: [default, cpq-net]
#   - and at the bottom:                                   networks: { cpq-net: { external: true } }
# Then: docker exec planningstool-caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# CAREFUL: on cpq-net the CPQ's Kong also answers to the short name "kong" (every
# compose service is known by its service name on each network it joins). This
# Caddy must therefore reach the planning tool's own Supabase by its container
# name (supabase-kong:8000), never by "kong:8000", or planning-api traffic lands
# on the CPQ's sign-in (happened on 5 Nov 2026).
#
# alleen_sleeve repeats the NSG in Caddy: should the NSG ever open up, the whole
# CPQ and its database still stay Sleeve only. Keep the addresses in step with
# NSG rules 121-123.

(alleen_sleeve) {
	@notsleeve not remote_ip 195.110.54.78/32 217.123.164.85/32 92.64.84.98/32
	respond @notsleeve 403
}

# --- internal entrance, for colleagues: the whole CPQ and its database ------------
cpq.sleevetechnology.com {
	import alleen_sleeve
	encode gzip
	handle_path /sb/* {
		reverse_proxy cpq-supabase-kong:8000
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy sleeve-cpq:3000 {
			transport http {
				read_timeout 120s
			}
		}
	}
}
